WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.312
Hi! Today you learn to tell the time.

2
00:00:06.712 --> 00:00:09.240
What time is it?

3
00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:15.189
What time is it? Listen:

4
00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:17.901
It's three o'clock.

5
00:00:18.301 --> 00:00:20.805
And now a trick:

6
00:00:21.205 --> 00:00:23.709
It's half past three.

7
00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:31.245
Halb vier means half an hour before four. So, three thirty!

8
00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:36.325
Careful, this is very important:

9
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:42.757
Halb elf is ten thirty. Not eleven thirty!

10
00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:48.003
In everyday speech we say nach (past) and vor (to):

11
00:00:48.403 --> 00:00:50.883
five past ten

12
00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.811
quarter past ten

13
00:00:54.211 --> 00:00:56.835
quarter to eleven

14
00:00:57.235 --> 00:00:59.667
five to eleven

15
00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:06.007
When does the class start? We say um:

16
00:01:06.407 --> 00:01:09.607
The class starts at eight.

17
00:01:10.007 --> 00:01:14.263
And how long? Von… bis (from… to):

18
00:01:14.663 --> 00:01:18.223
I work from nine to five.

19
00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:23.973
Listen: Mateo is in a hurry.

20
00:01:24.373 --> 00:01:26.901
What time is it?

21
00:01:27.301 --> 00:01:29.805
Quarter past eight.

22
00:01:30.205 --> 00:01:33.813
Oh no! The class!

23
00:01:34.213 --> 00:01:36.669
When does it start?

24
00:01:37.069 --> 00:01:39.333
At half past eight!

25
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:42.477
Then hurry, go!

26
00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:50.127
Now you! Look at the clock: what time is it now?

27
00:01:57.833 --> 00:02:01.969
Great! Now you can:

28
00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:07.969
You ask for the time and tell it – officially and in everyday speech.

29
00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:10.489
See you soon!
